    <!-- Challenges & Solutions -->
    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-title mb-4">Challenges & Solutions</h2>
        <div class="accordion accordion-flush" id="challengesAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-3">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#challenge1">
                        <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-2 text-warning"></i>
                        Type-Safe API Response Handling
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="challenge1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#challengesAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Ensuring runtime data matches expected TypeScript types from API responses.</p>
                        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Created a generic <code>IResponse&lt;T&gt;</code> interface that wraps all API responses with consistent structure. 
                        Implemented custom type guard functions to validate runtime data matches expected types before rendering.</p>
                        <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
                            <code class="small d-block">
                                data.data.every((item): item is ITask => '_id' in item && ...)
                            </code>
                            <p class="mb-0 mt-2 small">
                                The type guard uses TypeScript's 'is' keyword to narrow types, ensuring type safety at runtime while maintaining compile-time type checking.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-3">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#challenge2">
                        <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-2 text-warning"></i>
                        Form Validation with Runtime Type Checking
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="challenge2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#challengesAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Implementing robust form validation that works at both compile-time and runtime.</p>
                        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Integrated Zod schema validation with React Hook Form using @@hookform/resolvers. 
                        Created CreateTaskSchema that mirrors the ITask interface, providing both runtime validation and TypeScript inference.</p>
                        <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
                            <code class="small d-block">
                                z.infer&lt;typeof CreateTaskSchema&gt;
                            </code>
                            <p class="mb-0 mt-2 small">
                                The zodResolver automatically connects validation errors to form fields, displaying user-friendly error messages and eliminating type duplication.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border rounded mb-3">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#challenge3">
                        <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-2 text-warning"></i>
                        Synchronizing Client and Server State
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="challenge3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#challengesAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                        <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Keeping UI synchronized with backend data while providing instant user feedback.</p>
                        <p><strong>Solution:</strong> Leveraged TanStack Query's cache invalidation system to automatically refetch data after mutations. 
                        Implemented optimistic updates for immediate UI feedback while maintaining data consistency.</p>
                        <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
                            <code class="small d-block">
                                queryClient.invalidateQueries({ refetchType: 'all' })
                            </code>
                            <p class="mb-0 mt-2 small">
                                After each mutation (create/update), this ensures both active and inactive queries are refreshed, keeping task counters and task lists synchronized.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item border rounded">
                <h2 class="accordion-header">
                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#challenge4">
                        <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-2 text-warning"></i>
                        Date Handling Across Timezones
                    </button>
                </h2>
                <div id="challenge4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#challengesAccordion">
                    <div class="accordion-body">
